---
import Loading from '../../components/Loading.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---

<p class="h-load-intro">
  Each look plays its sequence once and holds the state the machine spent its
  busy time in. <button type="button" class="h-load-replay" data-h-load-replay>Replay them all</button>
</p>

<Specimen
  title="ZX Spectrum, tape"
  code={`<Loading machine="sinclair-zx-spectrum" showLabel />`}
  note="Two Emu198x captures of the 48K ROM, then drawn stripes (§7). Program: GAME once the header is read, the border white and then cyan as LD-BYTES waits for the data. Then the border is drawn: red and cyan for the pilot, 9.68 lines a band, blue and yellow for the data, 3.82 lines for a 0 bit and 7.63 for a 1, encoding the tape's real data block; the paper inside them is the capture's own. The stripes rise as the machine's did, at 15 lines a second rather than its 114, so no point of the border flashes more than twice a second (WCAG 2.3.1). Under reduced motion it is one still frame (§6)."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="sinclair-zx-spectrum" showLabel />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="Commodore 64, tape"
  code={`<Loading machine="commodore-64" showLabel />`}
  note="Emu198x captures of the stock KERNAL: PRESS PLAY ON TAPE, then the whole screen blanked to the border's light blue (drawn), FOUND GAME, then blanked again while it loads, which it holds. The KERNAL prints LOADING and blanks the screen on the same frame, so LOADING never shows during a tape load. No stripes: on the C64 those belonged to commercial turbo loaders."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="commodore-64" showLabel />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="Commodore 64, 1541 disk"
  code={`<Loading machine="commodore-64" media="disk" showLabel />`}
  note="Emu198x captures of the stock KERNAL and 1541 DOS: SEARCHING FOR GAME, then LOADING, on the normal blue screen; the 1541's red drive light lit. The guide names the light red; its hex is ours."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="commodore-64" media="disk" showLabel />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="Amiga 500, Kickstart 1.3"
  code={`<Loading machine="commodore-amiga" showLabel />`}
  note="COLOR00 as the 1.3 ROM writes it: dark grey $444, light grey $888, then white $FFF, with the drive light lit. White is the insert-disk screen's ground; Commodore's hand-and-disk picture is its artwork and is not drawn here. The drive light's colour, green, comes from a third-party book, and its hex is ours."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="commodore-amiga" showLabel />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="At twice the grid"
  code={`<Loading machine="commodore-64" media="disk" maxScale={2} />`}
  note="A whole multiple, like Screen: 2x where the cell is 832 pixels wide or more, 1x below that, and fitted to the cell only on a phone narrower than the grid (§7)."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="commodore-64" media="disk" maxScale={2} />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="NES: nothing to load"
  code={`<Loading machine="nintendo-entertainment-system" />   <!-- renders nothing -->`}
  note="A cartridge is mapped straight into the address space, so the machine never loaded and has no loading state. Loading renders nothing; show the content at once. The space below is deliberately empty."
  block
>
  <Loading machine="nintendo-entertainment-system" />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="A name the captures do not show"
  code={`<Loading machine="commodore-64" name="star trek" />
// [198x-ui] Loading: \`name\` was removed. The machine's messages are real captures of a
// program named GAME, and a capture cannot show another name. Put what is loading in \`label\`.`}
  note="Fails the build. The captures say GAME; putting another name in the status text is the honest way to say what is loading."
  block
></Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="A machine with no sourced look"
  code={`<Loading machine="bbc-micro" />
// [198x-ui] Loading: no sourced loading look for "bbc-micro". A loading state shows
// what that machine showed, quoted from a source, never borrowed from another machine (§7). …`}
  note="Fails the build. There is no default look, because any default would be another machine's. Add the machine to components/loading-looks.ts with its sources."
  block
></Specimen>

<script>
  /* Replay: re-insert every look so its sequence starts again. */
  document.querySelector('[data-h-load-replay]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    document.querySelectorAll('.h-load').forEach((el) => el.replaceWith(el.cloneNode(true)));
    (window as unknown as { fitLoads?: () => void }).fitLoads?.();
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .h-load-intro {
    margin: 0 0 var(--h-space-4);
    max-width: var(--h-measure);
    font-family: var(--h-font-read);
    font-size: var(--h-text-small);
    line-height: var(--h-lh-small);
    color: var(--h-ink-body);
  }
  .h-load-replay {
    min-height: 32px;
    padding: 0 var(--h-space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--h-line);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--h-shell);
    color: var(--h-ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-family: var(--h-font-ui);
    font-size: var(--h-text-micro);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .h-load-replay:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--h-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
